          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:11",
        "book": "Proverbs",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Now is she without, now in the streets, and lieth in wait at every corner.)",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "D&C 10:27 (26–27)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:12",
        "book": "Proverbs",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "So she caught him, and kissed him, and with an impudent face said unto him,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 38
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:13",
        "book": "Proverbs",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "I have peace offerings with me; this day have I payed my vows.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 1,
            "text": "IE She cynically suggests her piety."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 1,
            "end": 6
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:14",
        "book": "Proverbs",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore came I forth to meet thee, diligently to seek thy face, and I have found thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:15",
        "book": "Proverbs",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "I have decked my bed with coverings of tapestry, with carved works, with fine linen of Egypt.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:16",
        "book": "Proverbs",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "I have perfumed my bed with myrrh, aloes, and cinnamon.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "The Hebrew probably indicates a fragrant wood."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:17",
        "book": "Proverbs",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "Come, let us take our fill of love until the morning: let us solace ourselves with loves.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:18",
        "book": "Proverbs",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "For the goodman is not at home, he is gone a long journey:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 18
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:19",
        "book": "Proverbs",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "He hath taken a bag of money with him, and will come home at the day appointed.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 42
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:20",
        "book": "Proverbs",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "With her much fair speech she caused him to yield, with the flattering of her lips she forced him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:21",
        "book": "Proverbs",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "He goeth after her straightway, as an ox goeth to the slaughter, or as a fool to the correction of the stocks;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "OR suddenly; all at once."
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "TG Fornication."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Fornication.",
            "prettyString": "TG Fornication",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
